# Repos the SDK suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12,
# that gap was ~36 guards (a partial CI checkout ran 3444 passing / 40 pending
# where a full local checkout runs 3515 / 4). See test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js,
# which reports the surface this file leaves uncovered; the same gap applies
# to a sibling that is declared but missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# Drift gate (§8.5) over the mapped indexer handlers.
xchain-indexer
# Contract template parity (escrow, vesting, crowdsale, amm).
xchain-contracts
# Co-signer decode parity against the authoritative decoder.
xchain-decoder
# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity: BTC/LTC/DOGE/index/consensus_pin.
xchain-hub
# abi-core drift and the typed explorer-route contract.
xchain-explorer
# Consensus reference-impl parity and the canonical action map.
xchain-documentation
# The vendored roundtrip-conformance fixture.
xchain-encoder
# lint-core and metering vendored-copy parity.
xchain-vm
# Cross-repo consensus-constant byte-identity.
xchain-sync
# BIP44 derivation-path parity and the XCALL constant copy.
xchain-wallet
